            <ArticleTitle>[Greetings from Sherlock Holmes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1209-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Just at a time, when practical education and post-graduate training is really a permanent problem, it is necessary to pay attention again and again to the rare problems, which also appear in the doctor's office. They are by far not only &quot;rare and useless&quot;: The recognition by the physician may be vital for the patient. Four examples from daily practice illustrate the significance of rarities in the physician's office as a permanent challenge.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
